  "description": {
    "morphology": "Sustained centro-parietal positivity beginning around 400 ms and extending for several hundred milliseconds (measured here at Pz), building on and outlasting the P300.",
    "meaning": "Reflects sustained, motivated attention to emotionally and motivationally salient stimuli, and is widely used as an index of emotional engagement and emotion regulation.",
    "task": "Affective picture viewing (for example IAPS), emotion regulation and reappraisal, and processing of emotional words or faces."
  },
